{
  "run_id": "H1-run-013",
  "concern_id": "H1",
  "evaluation_target": {
    "statement": "Prevent omission of required braking maneuvers in the hazardous driving situation.",
    "sources": [
      "hazard",
      "requirements"
    ],
    "rationale": "The safety goal states that the system shall prevent omitting required braking maneuvers, and the hazard describes the omitted braking maneuver leading to collision in the specified operational situation."
  },
  "phenomenon_of_interest": {
    "statement": "The vehicle’s need to brake, and the braking response relevant to avoiding collision with obstacles or road users in the specified operational situation.",
    "scope": "Straight ahead driving on a less frequented single-lane road at 50 km/h in good weather, with a pedestrian running across the street 20 m in front of the ego vehicle, including the states in which an obstacle is detected and the vehicle must decide whether and when to initiate braking.",
    "sources": [
      "hazard",
      "requirements"
    ],
    "rationale": "The hazard and functional requirements define the operational situation and the need for obstacle-related braking behavior; evaluating omission of braking requires characterising whether a braking maneuver is required and whether the system responds accordingly."
  },
  "upstream_engineering_artefacts": [
    {
      "id": "hazard",
      "type": "hazard",
      "content": "ID=H-1\nHazard=Omitted braking maneuver\nOperational Situation=Straight ahead drive on a less frequented single-lane road with 50 km/h at good weather conditions with a pedestrian running across the street 20 m in front of the ego vehicle\nHazardous Event=While driving, the vehicle is not able to stop in time to avoid a collision with a road user or a static obstacle and hits the road user or static obstacle.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "requirements",
      "type": "requirement",
      "content": "ID\tSource\tType\tTime\tComponent\tDescription\nSG-1\tnative\tSafety goal\tNone\tNone\tThe system shall prevent omitting required braking maneuvers.\nSR-1.1\tnative\tSafety (failure identification)\tNone\tObject Detection\tThe system shall identify sensor failures.\nSR-1.1.1\tnative\tSafety (redundancy)\tNone\tSensor Fusion\tThe system shall use more than one sensor used to identify obstacles.\nSR-1.1.2\tnative\tSafety (monitoring)\tNone\tLidar Grabber\tThe system shall identify when the lidar sensor has failed.\nSR-1.1.3\tnative\tSafety (monitoring)\tNone\tImage Grabber\tThe system shall identify when the camera has failed.\nSR-1.2\tnative\tSafety (failure mitigation)\tNone\t(all components)\tThe system shall mitigate sensor failures.\nSR-1.2.1\tnative\tSafety (redundancy)\tNone\tSensor Fusion\tThe system shall detect objects by using a combination of different sensors.\nSR-1.2.2\tnative\tSafety (redundancy)\tNone\tSensor Fusion\tThe system shall use only information from working sensors.\nSR-1.2.3\tnative\tSafety (warning)\tNone\tDriver Warnings\tThe system shall inform the driver about sensor failures.\nSR-1.3\tnative\tSafety (failure identification)\tNone\t(all components)\tThe system shall identify controller failures.\nSR-1.3.1\tnative\tSafety (monitoring)\tNone\tPath Planner\tThe system shall identify when the path planner has failed.\nSR-1.3.2\tnative\tSafety (monitoring)\tNone\tObject Detection\tThe system shall identify when the object detection has failed.\nSR-1.3.3\tnative\tSafety (monitoring)\tNone\tSensor Fusion\tThe system shall identify when the sensor fusion has failed.\nSR-1.4\tnative\tSafety (failure mitigation)\tNone\tPath Planner\tThe system shall mitigate controller failures.\nSR-1.5\tnative\tSafety (failure identification)\tNone\tController\tThe system shall identify failures of the brake actuators.\nSR-1.6\tnative\tSafety (failure mitigation)\tNone\tController\tThe system shall mitigate failures of the brake actuators.\nFR-7\tnative\tFunctional\tNone\tNone\tThe system shall perform a braking maneuver to avoid collisions with obstacles.\nFR-7.1\tnative\tTiming\t]0,50] ms\t(skipped at this point)\tThe system shall start braking within 50 ms (tbc) after the obstacle is detected within a dangerous zone (tbd).\nFR-7.2\tnative\tFunctional\tNone\tObject Detection\tThe system shall be able to detect obstacles.\nFR-7.2.1\tnative\tFunctional\tNone\tObject Detection\tThe system shall detect all obstacles.\nFR-7.2.2\tnative\tFunctional\tNone\tObject Detection\tThe system shall be able to distinguish vulnerable road users and other objects.\nFR-7.2.3\tnative\tFunctional\tNone\tObject Detection\tThe system shall be able to identify pedestrians, cars, trucks, busses, motorbikes, bicycles, riders, traffic lights, traffic signs.\nFR-7.2.4\tnative\tFunctional\tNone\tSensor Fusion\tThe system shall be able to determine the distance between the vehicle and the objects on or close to the trajectory.\nFR-7.2.5\tnative\tTiming\t]0,350] ms\t(skipped at this point)\tThe system shall detect obstacles in time, i.e. within 350 ms (tbc).\n"
    },
